<fieldset class="card">
  <legend>
    <%= t("games.game_entries.legend") %>
  </legend>

  <ul class="game-list">
<%# entry.team / entry.game, not Team.find(entry.team_id) / Game.find(...).
    The finds ignored the associations and so could not be preloaded: two
    queries per entry, on top of the per-game ones the two controllers feeding
    this partial used to issue. Both now preload :team and :game
    (DashboardController#pending_entries_for, GamesController#show), which
    those finds would have thrown away.
    GameEntry declares both associations optional, so a row pointing at a
    deleted team reads nil here where find raised RecordNotFound -- both are a
    500 on this page, and validates :team_id, presence: true means the column
    itself is never blank. %>
<% game_entries.each do |entry| %>
  <li>
    <strong><%= entry.team.name %> <%= entry.game.name %></strong>
    <em><%= button_to t("games.game_entries.accept"), accept_game_entry_path(entry) %></em>
    <em><%= button_to t("games.game_entries.reject"), reject_game_entry_path(entry) %></em>
  </li>
<% end %>
</ul>
</fieldset>
